The legal texts come from LesLII, the Lesotho Legal Information Institute (supported by the Judiciary of Lesotho, the Law Office and the Law Society; on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  LesLII, https://lesotholii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as LesLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting LesLII as the source (https://lesotholii.org/terms-of-use/, read from the Internet Archive's copy).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: LesLII (https://lesotholii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws LesLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither LesLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Laws added on 2026-11-26 come from these sources, each with its own terms:

  Government of Lesotho, https://www.gov.ls (the Constitution of Lesotho 1993 and Orders No. 5 and 16 of
  1993, from https://www.gov.ls/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Lesotho_Constitution.pdf, retrieved 2026-11-26).
  Official text of Lesotho's law; the copy is marked "Government of Lesotho (c) All Rights Reserved-2000".

  WIPO Lex, World Intellectual Property Organization, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/ (retrieved 2026-11-26).
  WIPO Lex reproduces national laws for information; terms of use: https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html.
  Source: WIPO Lex.

  FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, https://www.fao.org/faolex/, PDFs at
  https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/, found through ECOLEX, https://www.ecolex.org (retrieved 2026-11-26).
  FAO's terms allow reproduction for non-commercial purposes with acknowledgement of FAO as the source
  (https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/en/). Source: FAOLEX (FAO).

  The Water Act, 2008 PDF in FAOLEX is Laws.Africa's: "There is no copyright on the legislative content";
  Laws.Africa's formatting is CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Source: Laws.Africa.

Changes made by Lexifina to these: the PDF's own text layer was read as is (no OCR by Lexifina), page
headers and page numbers were dropped, and each law was put in one file; the wording was not changed.
Neither FAO, WIPO nor the Government of Lesotho endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
